{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"destructuring","title":"Destructuring","group":"Arrays & Objects","order":26,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Unpack values from arrays and properties from objects into variables — with defaults, renaming, rest and nesting.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brackets\"></i>Array destructuring (by position)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const rgb = [255, 128, 0, 0.5];\nconst [red, green, , alpha = 1] = rgb;       // skip with a hole\nconsole.log(red, green, alpha);\nconst [head, ...tail] = \"hello\";             // any iterable\nconsole.log(head, tail);\nlet a = 1, b = 2;\n[a, b] = [b, a];                             // swap without a temp\nconsole.log(a, b);\nconst [x = 10, y = 20] = [undefined, null];  // default only for undefined\nconsole.log(x, y);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>255 128 0.5\nh [ 'e', 'l', 'l', 'o' ]\n2 1\n10 null</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-braces\"></i>Object destructuring (by name)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const user = { id: 7, name: \"Asha\", address: { city: \"Pune\", zip: \"411001\" } };\nconst { name, role = \"member\", id: userId } = user;          // default + rename\nconst { address: { city }, ...rest } = user;                 // nested + rest\nconsole.log(name, role, userId, city);\nconsole.log(rest);\nconst key = \"zip\";\nconst { [key]: zipCode } = user.address;                     // computed key\nconsole.log(zipCode);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Asha member 7 Pune\n{ id: 7, name: 'Asha' }\n411001</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-function\"></i>In function parameters and loops</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const format = ({ first, last = \"\", title = \"\" } = {}) =&gt; `${title} ${first} ${last}`.trim();\nconsole.log(format({ first: \"Ada\", last: \"Lovelace\", title: \"Countess\" }));\nconsole.log(format({ first: \"Linus\" }));\n\nconst entries = Object.entries({ a: 1, b: 2 });\nfor (const [key, value] of entries) console.log(key, value);\nconst points = [{ x: 1, y: 2 }, { x: 3, y: 4 }];\nconsole.log(points.map(({ x, y }) =&gt; x + y));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Countess Ada Lovelace\nLinus\na 1\nb 2\n[ 3, 7 ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>Pitfalls</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>try {\n  const { a } = null;\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.constructor.name);\n}\nlet value;\n({ value } = { value: 5 });   // parentheses needed when not declaring\nconsole.log(value);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>TypeError\n5</code></pre></figure>\n<ul><li>Destructuring <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> throws — give parameters a default <code>= {}</code>.</li><li>An assignment without <code>let</code>/<code>const</code> must be wrapped in <code>( )</code>, otherwise <code>{</code> starts a block.</li><li>Defaults apply only for <code>undefined</code>, never for <code>null</code>.</li></ul>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you swap two variables without a temporary?</summary><div><p><code>[a, b] = [b, a];</code> — the right side builds a temporary array, which is destructured back into the two names.</p></div></details></section>"}